        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x-6)^2+(y-7)^2=36$",
          "worked": "The radius is the perpendicular distance from $(6,7)$ to the $y$-axis, so $r=6$.\n$$\\begin{align*}(x-6)^2+(y-7)^2&=6^2\\\\(x-6)^2+(y-7)^2&=36\\end{align*}$$",
